Definedness is fixed, but the term remains non-constructor and therefore never becomes a syntactic `KResult`; the generic BoolOp rules cannot match it. I’m adding the narrow guarded BoolOp dispatch twins endorsed by the projection pattern: for `isStrV(V) and REST`, continue under the true guard and return `false` under the false guard. They are exact specializations of the two frozen short-circuit rules and expose no new value.
