The isolated trace reveals the real explosion: the symbolic type guard is narrowing `V:Val` across every value constructor, even though the theorem only needs a two-way string/non-string split. I’m changing the exact type tag to the Kit’s opaque-total proof representation: ground `[concrete]` equations retain the frozen predicate’s behavior, while the existing universal `#Ceil(Val ⇒ Str)` characterization fixes the symbolic tag as cast definedness. This should produce two symbolic branches without enumerating all `Val` constructors.
